# Normalize every text file to LF on checkout, regardless of the checking-
# out machine's core.autocrlf setting -- a CRLF-converted .sh/.env breaks
# bash ($'\r': command not found, or "bad interpreter" on the shebang
# line), and core.autocrlf=true is a common Windows/WSL git default that
# would otherwise convert files silently. Enumerating extensions one at a
# time missed .env.example, .gitignore, .python-version, and uv.lock the
# first time around, so this is a blanket rule instead: git's own
# content-based detection decides what counts as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary as a safety net, in case that auto-detection ever
# misjudges these.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
